1. Her father, whom she calls "Papa Elia," was a trumpet player and allowed her to play brass instruments because of his own background. (Verbatim: "Papa Elia was actually okay with that, because the reason I played brass instruments, and the reason I was allowed to, is because Papa Elia used to play brass instruments. He was a trumpet player, so he was actually okay with that.")

2. She played the French horn to grade six level in the ABRSM music examination system but did not reach grade eight. (Verbatim: "I was grade six, which isn't fantastic to be honest. I never got to grade eight, which is like the maximum grade for the ABRSM.")

3. She was first chair in an orchestra but disliked the experience. (Verbatim: "But I was first chair, but I hated it.")

4. She owns a French horn that is currently rusty and needs tuning and maintenance. (Verbatim: "The problem is it's actually, I could just whack it out. Like, but it's very rusty and I feel like I should buy something to de-rust it and it needs tuning.")

5. She is considering or expressing interest in doing a French horn streaming series. (Verbatim: "You want my 3am French horn stream? I would, honestly, if it wasn't so late right now, I would whack out the French horn.")

6. She associates her current favorite color with purple, saying "it's my color now." (Verbatim: "Um, you know, but it's my color now. Purple.")

7. She has experience playing melodic instruments and refers to her setup as "Elia's Piano Bar, a.k.a. Elia's Melodica Bar." (Verbatim: "Welcome, welcome to Elia's Piano Bar, a.k.a. Elia's Melodica Bar.")

8. She believes the timbre of a French horn reflects the player's skill and experience, and that electronic versions cannot replicate its personality. (Verbatim: "The timbre of which the French horn has varies based on how much experience the French horn player has... you wouldn't be able to do that because there's so much personality when you play the French horn.")

9. She mentions the challenge of playing the French horn on stream due to its reflective surface causing glare. (Verbatim: "I need, like, just play piano instead. Oh my god, you can buy it and it's cool. Wear a mask? That doesn't cover me fully.")

10. She previously found old sheet music and film-related items in her French horn case before throwing them away. (Verbatim: "I found some sheet music in my... what do you call it? In my French horn case, but I threw it away. I had some film stuff, like, yeah, like, mmm, mmm, mmm.") [end of text]



1. She plays the melodica and associates time spent with her audience with playing it. (Verbatim: "And by 'spend time with me', I mean 'spend time with me while I play the melodica', like, 'cause that's what I want to do right now.")

2. She struggles with reading piano sheet music and finds it difficult to play by ear. (Verbatim: "Like I can recognize the notes, but my fingers just don't know where to go because I really suck at piano.")

3. She is envious of people who can play music by ear, especially her little brother who has that skill. (Verbatim: "My little brother has that skill I'm jealous of anybody that does have that skill... I am so incredibly jealous of you because my ear sucks.")

4. She dislikes complex key signatures in sheet music, particularly those with many sharps. (Verbatim: "When I see a scary key signature I die" / "three hashtags those hashtags make me sad.")

5. She has a strong preference for treble clef and dislikes bass clef. (Verbatim: "bass clef can go in the bin" / "don't you talk badly about my heckin treble clef.")

6. She enjoys music from *The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time*, especially "Song of Storms" and Kakariko Village theme. (Verbatim: "love the Zelda music it sounded like one in the ocarina of time" / "what'd you call it um kakriko kak the village... Kakariko village sheet music.")

7. She is interested in playing the Wii Shop Channel theme music on melodica. (Verbatim: "I want to do that one next yeah yeah yeah yeah... wii shop menu is that it is that it i want to do that one next.")

8. She expresses frustration with SVG file formats when trying to access sheet music. (Verbatim: "what's a heckin svg file what am i supposed to do with this make it png oh my god that didn't work.")

9. She values audience presence over monetary support. (Verbatim: "I don't want your money. I want you to spend time with me.")

10. She refers to herself in a playful, self-deprecating manner regarding her musical abilities. (Verbatim: "i can give you um slightly okay streamer that's trying her bestest.") [end of text]



